{"parentUuid":"3bbaa059-678a-4d65-99f5-0e74eeba3575","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1aa1a67f-cc4a-49b5-9b55-04ec3c1fcd6d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Base directory for this skill: /Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/startup\n\n# Startup\n\nThe front door for a work session on either machine. This skill owns no logic of its own — it runs `dev-sync`, whose Step 5 loads context back in.\n\n## What to do\n\nInvoke the `dev-sync` skill and run it end to end, Step 0 through Step 5.\n\nDo not reimplement any of it here. If the sync behaviour or the context report needs to change, change `dev-sync/SKILL.md`. One home for the procedure, and this file is an alias so the command matches how Eric actually thinks about it: \"sync\" is what the machine does, \"startup\" is what he is doing.\n\n## After the report\n\n`dev-sync` Step 5 ends with a short \"picking up\" report and a stop. Hold there and wait for Eric to confirm or redirect. Do not begin the next task on your own — `docs/STATUS.md` records where the last session stopped, which is not the same as what he wants to do this morning.\n\nIf he names a repo when he invokes this, pass it through so Step 5 reports on that one instead of guessing from the most recent commit.\n\n## Not this\n\n- Not the morning brief. Calendar, email and the shape of the day belong to the `morning` / `morning-briefing` work. This skill answers \"where was I\", not \"what's my day\".\n- Not a memory loader. Global memory arrives through the SessionStart hook before this runs; do not re-read `USER.md` or `MEMORY.md` by hand.\n"}]},"isMeta":true,"turnCompanion":true,"uuid":"9af73614-6a4b-461e-b0b1-b669167bf584","timestamp":"2026-09-12T04:09:26.939Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills","sessionId":"ca9f8ae1-3064-4ead-9a52-e1c579c0f997","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","sessionKind":"bg"}
