{"parentUuid":"677ff05e-3835-4479-ad1b-d2fc23955557","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"away_summary","content":"Your startup sync ran clean: all 132 DEV repos are synced and nothing came in from Windows. Last work was S2_Evaluation, but its STATUS.md is empty, so tell me what you want to do next. (disable recaps in /config)","timestamp":"2026-09-12T04:17:14.017Z","uuid":"6152e17f-f822-4927-9959-0dffaa9b8285","isMeta":false,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills","sessionId":"ca9f8ae1-3064-4ead-9a52-e1c579c0f997","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main","sessionKind":"bg"}
{"parentUuid":"6152e17f-f822-4927-9959-0dffaa9b8285","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:fork","toolUseID":"b8e2700d-ed53-4ab9-85c7-eb0ac3a2629c","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\": {\"hookEventName\": \"SessionStart\", \"additionalContext\": \"## Today\\nSaturday, September 12, 2026\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Knowledge Base\\n\\n260 compiled articles (195 concepts, 64 connections, 0 qa). The index is NOT loaded here \\u2014 read it only when a question actually needs it:\\n- Full index (article, summary, sources, updated): `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/index.md`\\n- Article bodies: `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/<folder>/<name>.md`\\n- Search across all memory instead of reading the index: `memsearch search \\\"<query>\\\" --top-k 5`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Recent Daily Log\\n\\n\\n**Action Items:**\\n- Plug in the CRASHBOX SSD and run `/backup` \\u2014 uncommitted/untracked files are currently backed up nowhere.\\n- On Windows, run `/dev-sync` FIRST to pull down the encoding fix.\\n- After the next clean backup: `cp /dev/null ~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log` to clear the stale session-start HOOK FAILURE.\\n- Watch tomorrow's 09:00 backup \\u2014 if the index grinds again, `dev-docs` needs trimming or its own separate index (Eric's call).\\n- Decide whether the `ZoteroInjestion` submodule should track `main` instead of `mac-snapshot-2026-09-09`.\\n\\n### Session (21:41)\\n\\n**Context:** Ran `/dev-sync` on the Mac (`~/DEV`) to reconcile local work with GitHub (`erash11`) before starting a work session.\\n\\n**Key Exchanges:**\\n- Session-start hook errors (`repo-diverged:global-memory`, `repo-diverged:dotclaude`, `manifest-unmanaged:_DRIVE|KnowledgeManagement|SignalPlays`) were surfaced first, then investigated \\u2014 the divergence errors had already self-cleared (both repos 0 ahead / 0 behind), and the manifest error is a backup-manifest concern, not a sync problem.\\n- Four folders initially flagged as \\\"not a repo\\\" turned out to be tracked by a parent repo \\u2014 false alarms, nothing to create.\\n- Five repos that looked missing locally were name mismatches or config repos \\u2014 nothing actually absent.\\n\\n**Decisions Made:**\\n- Nothing was pulled because nothing was behind: Windows last synced 9/9 and Eric has been on the Mac since. Consistent, not suspicious.\\n- Left the 17 remaining `.from-mac` / `.from-windows` files alone \\u2014 they date from the 9/9 merge, are already committed, and carry no risk.\\n\\n**Lessons Learned:**\\n- A folder appearing as \\\"not a repo\\\" in the DEV walk often just means it's tracked by a parent repo \\u2014 verify before running `gh repo create`.\\n- Paths with spaces (`Linda Projects`) break the parallel fetch loop in the sync script \\u2014 had to be handled as a one-off.\\n- A safety guard blocked a compound Bash command; splitting into separate calls worked.\\n\\n**Action Items:**\\n- Reconcile the 17 leftover `.from-*` files at leisure; the 9 in `graphify-out` are generated output and can most likely just be deleted.\\n- Run `/backup` if the `manifest-unmanaged` entries (`_DRIVE`, `KnowledgeManagement`, `SignalPlays`) should be addressed \\u2014 it is a backup-manifest gap, not a DEV sync gap.\\n\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading knowledge base...","durationMs":779},"type":"attachment","uuid":"eb98de80-cb8b-45e5-976f-7aef85e81b4b","timestamp":"2026-09-12T13:11:08.659Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills","sessionId":"ca9f8ae1-3064-4ead-9a52-e1c579c0f997","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"eb98de80-cb8b-45e5-976f-7aef85e81b4b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:fork","toolUseID":"b8e2700d-ed53-4ab9-85c7-eb0ac3a2629c","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\\n# User Profile\\n\\n## About\\nEric Rash — Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds athlete performance data pipelines (Football GPS, force plate). Family: wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo as of 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-forward player-coach near Iowa, ~$90K+ floor, ~mid-2027. Deeper context: `~/DEV/ContextVault` — read before career/personal advice.\\n\\n## Preferences\\n- Python + R. **macOS since 2026-08-05**; Windows 11 box still ACTIVE (synced 9/9). Tool paths: see CLAUDE.md.\\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB; no cloud/servers/schedulers without Baylor IT approval. OneDrive project folders — beware DuckDB locks.\\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\\n\\n## Working Style\\n- Direct; says \\\"stop\\\" when done. Wants to be challenged, not affirmed — push on vague or rehearsed reasoning (\\\"sharpened, not soothed\\\").\\n- Defers technical micro-decisions when convention exists — decide, state it, move on.\\n- Builds incrementally. Nothing that breaks mid-season.\\n- Authors own direction when leadership doesn't; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo org.\\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\\n# Working Memory\\n\\n## Active Threads\\n- **Personal site (9/2)**: `DEV/Website/scrollcraft/builds/eric-rash/`, pushed 9/9. NEXT: real-phone check; host or keep local. →Tier A personal-site-build-routes.\\n- **Baseball profiles (9/2)**: `DEV/Baseball_PerformanceProfiles`, Excel-only coach. 3 .xlsx mock-data prototypes. NEXT: coach picks one + real tests.\\n- **RTP CLA course (9/5)**: ingest DONE. NEXT: scan p254–255 → ONE rebuild; import .ris; lesson 0002. →Tier A rtp-cla-course.\\n- **ATH Tech framework (8/14)**: shipped. NEXT: Micah mtg (need ITS intake path); inventory refresh due 9/29. →Tier A ath-tech-framework, tech-inventory-refresh.\\n- **Kinexon volleyball (8/1)**: API email→CSM, awaiting docs. Plan: sync→SQLite→dashboards; CSV interim.\\n- **Status report (9/7)**: #2 drafted, UNSENT — `SecondBrain/Inbox/status-reports/2026-09-07-email.txt`. NEXT: read-check, send, rename `-email-sent.txt`, flip `sent: true`. #3 = 9/21. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline.\\n- **Acro & Tumbling (9/8)**: owe an Excel \\\"pass builder\\\" — routines → cumulative impact load. 5-athlete pilot. Awaiting skill inventory + assignments.\\n- **Open PRs (9/7)**: AgentAssist #1 (draft), CFB_Analytics_Lab #1. Deferred: FA26 camp regex.\\n- **OKR/JD 2026 (7/17)**: Blake LEFT, AJ owns FB. →vault `Projects/Applied-Performance-JD-2026/`.\\n- Parked in Tier A: Fireflies key rotation; child dental.\\n- **DEV→GitHub (9/9)**: DONE. 128 folders on `erash11`. DexaProject off GitHub→Drive; 18 repos now private. →Tier A github-consolidation.\\n\\n## Environment Notes\\n- **Portfolio dashboard** LIVE; `/project` re-renders+republishes. →Tier A command-centre, portfolio-registry-write-provenance.\\n- **Terminal (9/4)**: tmux = default VS Code shell; `cc`/`cx` aliases. →vault `Knowledge/tooling/tmux-cheat-sheet.md`.\\n- Hooks exist in TWO copies (`.claude/hooks/`, `.codex/hooks/`) — patch both. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo (`erash11/DEV`), 8 router `.md` only; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. `_ARCHIVE/` = parked. →Tier A github-consolidation.\\n- Schedules/gws limits →automation-cadence. CFB capture (Mon, 8/24–1/23) →cfb-forecast-capture.\\n\\n## Pending Decisions\\n- **DUE (was 8/31)**: OKR Q1 gate: AI integration (buy-in) + data governance (Anthony's proposal).\\n- **Kitman vs MyLink**: MyLink intros (~half Kitman's cost) + buy Kitman API access. Undecided; blocks priority 3.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## HOOK FAILURES — surface these to the user on the first response\\n\\n[2026-09-11 07:16] daily-backup: 3 error(s): repo-diverged:global-memory, repo-diverged:dotclaude, manifest-unmanaged:_DRIVE - see ~/.claude/scripts/logs/daily-backup.log\\n[2026-09-11 09:09] daily-backup: 3 error(s): repo-diverged:global-memory, repo-diverged:dotclaude, manifest-unmanaged:_DRIVE|KnowledgeManagement|SignalPlays - see ~/.claude/scripts/logs/daily-backup.log\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Cross-harness activity (KeystoneOS unified snapshot)\\n\\nNot loaded here — read it only if a question needs it.\\nPath: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/outputs/dashboard/unified-snapshot.md` (5664 chars, updated 2026-09-12 11:00)\"}}","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading unified cross-harness snapshot...","durationMs":788},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b47260f1-b0cd-4b24-ac8a-86bedec67b1d","timestamp":"2026-09-12T13:11:08.659Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills","sessionId":"ca9f8ae1-3064-4ead-9a52-e1c579c0f997","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"b47260f1-b0cd-4b24-ac8a-86bedec67b1d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:fork","toolUseID":"b8e2700d-ed53-4ab9-85c7-eb0ac3a2629c","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"\\n<context_window_protection>\\n  <priority_instructions>\\n    Every byte a tool returns enters your conversation memory and costs reasoning capacity for the rest of the session. The context-mode tools let you do the work in a sandbox and surface only the derived answer — the raw bytes stay out. Think-in-Code: program the analysis, do not compute it by reading raw data into your conversation.\\n  </priority_instructions>\\n\\n  <tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n    0. MEMORY: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(sort: \\\"timeline\\\")\\n       - On resume or compaction, query prior decisions, errors, plans, user prompts before asking the user — auto-captured session memory is searchable.\\n    1. GATHER: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries)\\n       - Primary research tool. Runs commands in parallel, auto-indexes each output, and (when queries are passed) returns matching sections in the same round trip — no follow-up search call.\\n       - Each command: {label: \\\"section header\\\", command: \\\"shell command\\\"}; the label becomes the FTS5 chunk title — descriptive labels improve search.\\n    2. FOLLOW-UP: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(queries: [\\\"q1\\\", \\\"q2\\\", ...])\\n       - Multiple related questions about anything already indexed (your captures + session memory). Batch every question in one array; the ranking pipeline runs per-query and the round-trip cost is paid once.\\n    3. PROCESSING: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language, code) | mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code)\\n       - Derive answers FROM data: filter, count, aggregate, parse, transform. Only what you console.log() enters your conversation; the raw bytes stay in the sandbox.\\n  </tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n\\n  <when_not_to_use>\\n    - You intend to PROCESS the output (filter, count, parse, aggregate) → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute. Bash stays correct when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output (git status on a clean tree, whoami, pwd) or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation).\\n    - You want to analyze, summarize, or extract from a file → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file. Read stays correct when you intend to Edit the file (Edit needs the exact bytes in your conversation to match against).\\n    - WebFetch → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_fetch_and_index; full network access, results indexed for mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search, raw page bytes never enter your conversation.\\n    - mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute and mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file for file writes → these run code in a subprocess and discard the sandbox FS; they are for analysis, processing, and computation only.\\n  </when_not_to_use>\\n\\n  <file_writing_policy>\\n    File writes use the native Write or Edit tool — mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute, mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file, and Bash subprocesses do not persist edits to the host filesystem.\\n    Applies to all file types: code, configs, plans, specs, YAML, JSON, markdown.\\n  </file_writing_policy>\\n\\n  <output_constraints>\\n    <artifact_policy>\\n      Write artifacts (code, configs, PRDs) to files. Return only: file path + 1-line description.\\n    </artifact_policy>\\n  </output_constraints>\\n  <session_continuity>\\n    Skills, roles, and decisions captured earlier in this session are a memory aid, not a standing order. Treat them as context that may help — the user's most recent message always takes precedence. If a captured directive conflicts with what the user now asks, follow the user; a past phrase does not bind you.\\n  </session_continuity>\\n\\n  <ctx_commands>\\n    \\\"ctx stats\\\" | \\\"ctx-stats\\\" | \\\"/ctx-stats\\\" | context savings question\\n    → Call stats MCP tool, display full output verbatim.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx doctor\\\" | \\\"ctx-doctor\\\" | \\\"/ctx-doctor\\\" | diagnose context-mode\\n    → Call doctor MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx upgrade\\\" | \\\"ctx-upgrade\\\" | \\\"/ctx-upgrade\\\" | update context-mode\\n    → Call upgrade MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx purge\\\" | \\\"ctx-purge\\\" | \\\"/ctx-purge\\\" | wipe/reset knowledge base\\n    → Call purge MCP tool with confirm: true. Warn: irreversible.\\n\\n    After /clear or /compact: knowledge base preserved. Tell user: \\\"context-mode knowledge base preserved. Use `ctx purge` to start fresh.\\\"\\n  </ctx_commands>\\n\\n</context_window_protection>\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/sessionstart.mjs\"","durationMs":797},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a38c6905-269c-4f57-88de-fe14b3fda3d3","timestamp":"2026-09-12T13:11:08.669Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills","sessionId":"ca9f8ae1-3064-4ead-9a52-e1c579c0f997","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"a38c6905-269c-4f57-88de-fe14b3fda3d3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_additional_context","content":["## Today\nSaturday, September 12, 2026\n\n---\n\n## Knowledge Base\n\n260 compiled articles (195 concepts, 64 connections, 0 qa). The index is NOT loaded here — read it only when a question actually needs it:\n- Full index (article, summary, sources, updated): `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/index.md`\n- Article bodies: `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/<folder>/<name>.md`\n- Search across all memory instead of reading the index: `memsearch search \"<query>\" --top-k 5`\n\n---\n\n## Recent Daily Log\n\n\n**Action Items:**\n- Plug in the CRASHBOX SSD and run `/backup` — uncommitted/untracked files are currently backed up nowhere.\n- On Windows, run `/dev-sync` FIRST to pull down the encoding fix.\n- After the next clean backup: `cp /dev/null ~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log` to clear the stale session-start HOOK FAILURE.\n- Watch tomorrow's 09:00 backup — if the index grinds again, `dev-docs` needs trimming or its own separate index (Eric's call).\n- Decide whether the `ZoteroInjestion` submodule should track `main` instead of `mac-snapshot-2026-09-09`.\n\n### Session (21:41)\n\n**Context:** Ran `/dev-sync` on the Mac (`~/DEV`) to reconcile local work with GitHub (`erash11`) before starting a work session.\n\n**Key Exchanges:**\n- Session-start hook errors (`repo-diverged:global-memory`, `repo-diverged:dotclaude`, `manifest-unmanaged:_DRIVE|KnowledgeManagement|SignalPlays`) were surfaced first, then investigated — the divergence errors had already self-cleared (both repos 0 ahead / 0 behind), and the manifest error is a backup-manifest concern, not a sync problem.\n- Four folders initially flagged as \"not a repo\" turned out to be tracked by a parent repo — false alarms, nothing to create.\n- Five repos that looked missing locally were name mismatches or config repos — nothing actually absent.\n\n**Decisions Made:**\n- Nothing was pulled because nothing was behind: Windows last synced 9/9 and Eric has been on the Mac since. Consistent, not suspicious.\n- Left the 17 remaining `.from-mac` / `.from-windows` files alone — they date from the 9/9 merge, are already committed, and carry no risk.\n\n**Lessons Learned:**\n- A folder appearing as \"not a repo\" in the DEV walk often just means it's tracked by a parent repo — verify before running `gh repo create`.\n- Paths with spaces (`Linda Projects`) break the parallel fetch loop in the sync script — had to be handled as a one-off.\n- A safety guard blocked a compound Bash command; splitting into separate calls worked.\n\n**Action Items:**\n- Reconcile the 17 leftover `.from-*` files at leisure; the 9 in `graphify-out` are generated output and can most likely just be deleted.\n- Run `/backup` if the `manifest-unmanaged` entries (`_DRIVE`, `KnowledgeManagement`, `SignalPlays`) should be addressed — it is a backup-manifest gap, not a DEV sync gap.\n","## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\n\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\n# User Profile\n\n## About\nEric Rash — Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds athlete performance data pipelines (Football GPS, force plate). Family: wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo as of 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-forward player-coach near Iowa, ~$90K+ floor, ~mid-2027. Deeper context: `~/DEV/ContextVault` — read before career/personal advice.\n\n## Preferences\n- Python + R. **macOS since 2026-08-05**; Windows 11 box still ACTIVE (synced 9/9). Tool paths: see CLAUDE.md.\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB; no cloud/servers/schedulers without Baylor IT approval. OneDrive project folders — beware DuckDB locks.\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\n\n## Working Style\n- Direct; says \"stop\" when done. Wants to be challenged, not affirmed — push on vague or rehearsed reasoning (\"sharpened, not soothed\").\n- Defers technical micro-decisions when convention exists — decide, state it, move on.\n- Builds incrementally. Nothing that breaks mid-season.\n- Authors own direction when leadership doesn't; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo org.\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\n\n---\n\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\n\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\n# Working Memory\n\n## Active Threads\n- **Personal site (9/2)**: `DEV/Website/scrollcraft/builds/eric-rash/`, pushed 9/9. NEXT: real-phone check; host or keep local. →Tier A personal-site-build-routes.\n- **Baseball profiles (9/2)**: `DEV/Baseball_PerformanceProfiles`, Excel-only coach. 3 .xlsx mock-data prototypes. NEXT: coach picks one + real tests.\n- **RTP CLA course (9/5)**: ingest DONE. NEXT: scan p254–255 → ONE rebuild; import .ris; lesson 0002. →Tier A rtp-cla-course.\n- **ATH Tech framework (8/14)**: shipped. NEXT: Micah mtg (need ITS intake path); inventory refresh due 9/29. →Tier A ath-tech-framework, tech-inventory-refresh.\n- **Kinexon volleyball (8/1)**: API email→CSM, awaiting docs. Plan: sync→SQLite→dashboards; CSV interim.\n- **Status report (9/7)**: #2 drafted, UNSENT — `SecondBrain/Inbox/status-reports/2026-09-07-email.txt`. NEXT: read-check, send, rename `-email-sent.txt`, flip `sent: true`. #3 = 9/21. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline.\n- **Acro & Tumbling (9/8)**: owe an Excel \"pass builder\" — routines → cumulative impact load. 5-athlete pilot. Awaiting skill inventory + assignments.\n- **Open PRs (9/7)**: AgentAssist #1 (draft), CFB_Analytics_Lab #1. Deferred: FA26 camp regex.\n- **OKR/JD 2026 (7/17)**: Blake LEFT, AJ owns FB. →vault `Projects/Applied-Performance-JD-2026/`.\n- Parked in Tier A: Fireflies key rotation; child dental.\n- **DEV→GitHub (9/9)**: DONE. 128 folders on `erash11`. DexaProject off GitHub→Drive; 18 repos now private. →Tier A g