ex is NOT loaded here — read it only when a question actually needs it:\n- Full index (article, summary, sources, updated): `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/index.md`\n- Article bodies: `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/<folder>/<name>.md`\n- Search across all memory instead of reading the index: `memsearch search \"<query>\" --top-k 5`\n\n---\n\n## Recent Daily Log\n\n\n**Action Items:**\n- Plug in the CRASHBOX SSD and run `/backup` — uncommitted/untracked files are currently backed up nowhere.\n- On Windows, run `/dev-sync` FIRST to pull down the encoding fix.\n- After the next clean backup: `cp /dev/null ~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log` to clear the stale session-start HOOK FAILURE.\n- Watch tomorrow's 09:00 backup — if the index grinds again, `dev-docs` needs trimming or its own separate index (Eric's call).\n- Decide whether the `ZoteroInjestion` submodule should track `main` instead of `mac-snapshot-2026-09-09`.\n\n### Session (21:41)\n\n**Context:** Ran `/dev-sync` on the Mac (`~/DEV`) to reconcile local work with GitHub (`erash11`) before starting a work session.\n\n**Key Exchanges:**\n- Session-start hook errors (`repo-diverged:global-memory`, `repo-diverged:dotclaude`, `manifest-unmanaged:_DRIVE|KnowledgeManagement|SignalPlays`) were surfaced first, then investigated — the divergence errors had already self-cleared (both repos 0 ahead / 0 behind), and the manifest error is a backup-manifest concern, not a sync problem.\n- Four folders initially flagged as \"not a repo\" turned out to be tracked by a parent repo — false alarms, nothing to create.\n- Five repos that looked missing locally were name mismatches or config repos — nothing actually absent.\n\n**Decisions Made:**\n- Nothing was pulled because nothing was behind: Windows last synced 9/9 and Eric has been on the Mac since. Consistent, not suspicious.\n- Left the 17 remaining `.from-mac` / `.from-windows` files alone — they date from the 9/9 merge, are already committed, and carry no risk.\n\n**Lessons Learned:**\n- A folder appearing as \"not a repo\" in the DEV walk often just means it's tracked by a parent repo — verify before running `gh repo create`.\n- Paths with spaces (`Linda Projects`) break the parallel fetch loop in the sync script — had to be handled as a one-off.\n- A safety guard blocked a compound Bash command; splitting into separate calls worked.\n\n**Action Items:**\n- Reconcile the 17 leftover `.from-*` files at leisure; the 9 in `graphify-out` are generated output and can most likely just be deleted.\n- Run `/backup` if the `manifest-unmanaged` entries (`_DRIVE`, `KnowledgeManagement`, `SignalPlays`) should be addressed — it is a backup-manifest gap, not a DEV sync gap.\n\n## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\n\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\n# User Profile\n\n## About\nEric Rash — Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds athlete performance data pipelines (Football GPS, force plate). Family: wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo as of 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-forward player-coach near Iowa, ~$90K+ floor, ~mid-2027. Deeper context: `~/DEV/ContextVault` — read before career/personal advice.\n\n## Preferences\n- Python + R. **macOS since 2026-08-05**; Windows 11 box still ACTIVE (synced 9/9). Tool paths: see CLAUDE.md.\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB; no cloud/servers/schedulers without Baylor IT approval. OneDrive project folders — beware DuckDB locks.\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\n\n## Working Style\n- Direct; says \"stop\" when done. Wants to be challenged, not affirmed — push on vague or rehearsed reasoning (\"sharpened, not soothed\").\n- Defers technical micro-decisions when convention exists — decide, state it, move on.\n- Builds incrementally. Nothing that breaks mid-season.\n- Authors own direction when leadership doesn't; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo org.\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\n\n---\n\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\n\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\n# Working Memory\n\n## Active Threads\n- **Personal site (9/2)**: `DEV/Website/scrollcraft/builds/eric-rash/`, pushed 9/9. NEXT: real-phone check; host or keep local. →Tier A personal-site-build-routes.\n- **Baseball profiles (9/2)**: `DEV/Baseball_PerformanceProfiles`, Excel-only coach. 3 .xlsx mock-data prototypes. NEXT: coach picks one + real tests.\n- **RTP CLA course (9/5)**: ingest DONE. NEXT: scan p254–255 → ONE rebuild; import .ris; lesson 0002. →Tier A rtp-cla-course.\n- **ATH Tech framework (8/14)**: shipped. NEXT: Micah mtg (need ITS intake path); inventory refresh due 9/29. →Tier A ath-tech-framework, tech-inventory-refresh.\n- **Kinexon volleyball (8/1)**: API email→CSM, awaiting docs. Plan: sync→SQLite→dashboards; CSV interim.\n- **Status report (9/7)**: #2 drafted, UNSENT — `SecondBrain/Inbox/status-reports/2026-09-07-email.txt`. NEXT: read-check, send, rename `-email-sent.txt`, flip `sent: true`. #3 = 9/21. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline.\n- **Acro & Tumbling (9/8)**: owe an Excel \"pass builder\" — routines → cumulative impact load. 5-athlete pilot. Awaiting skill inventory + assignments.\n- **Open PRs (9/7)**: AgentAssist #1 (draft), CFB_Analytics_Lab #1. Deferred: FA26 camp regex.\n- **OKR/JD 2026 (7/17)**: Blake LEFT, AJ owns FB. →vault `Projects/Applied-Performance-JD-2026/`.\n- Parked in Tier A: Fireflies key rotation; child dental.\n- **DEV→GitHub (9/9)**: DONE. 128 folders on `erash11`. DexaProject off GitHub→Drive; 18 repos now private. →Tier A github-consolidation.\n\n## Environment Notes\n- **Portfolio dashboard** LIVE; `/project` re-renders+republishes. →Tier A command-centre, portfolio-registry-write-provenance.\n- **Terminal (9/4)**: tmux = default VS Code shell; `cc`/`cx` aliases. →vault `Knowledge/tooling/tmux-cheat-sheet.md`.\n- Hooks exist in TWO copies (`.claude/hooks/`, `.codex/hooks/`) — patch both. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo (`erash11/DEV`), 8 router `.md` only; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. `_ARCHIVE/` = parked. →Tier A github-consolidation.\n- Schedules/gws limits →automation-cadence. CFB capture (Mon, 8/24–1/23) →cfb-forecast-capture.\n\n## Pending Decisions\n- **DUE (was 8/31)**: OKR Q1 gate: AI integration (buy-in) + data governance (Anthony's proposal).\n- **Kitman vs MyLink**: MyLink intros (~half Kitman's cost) + buy Kitman API access. Undecided; blocks priority 3.\n\n---\n\n## HOOK FAILURES — surface these to the user on the first response\n\n[2026-09-11 07:16] daily-backup: 3 error(s): repo-diverged:global-memory, repo-diverged:dotclaude, manifest-unmanaged:_DRIVE - see ~/.claude/scripts/logs/daily-backup.log\n[2026-09-11 09:09] daily-backup: 3 error(s): repo-diverged:global-memory, repo-diverged:dotclaude, manifest-unmanaged:_DRIVE|KnowledgeManagement|SignalPlays - see ~/.claude/scripts/logs/daily-backup.log\n\n---\n\n## Cross-harness activity (KeystoneOS unified snapshot)\n\nNot loaded here — read it only if a question needs it.\nPath: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/outputs/dashboard/unified-snapshot.md` (5664 chars, updated 2026-09-12 11:00)\n</system-reminder>"}],"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills","sessionId":"ca9f8ae1-3064-4ead-9a52-e1c579c0f997","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"8b3dd69e-fb72-4462-b8a7-b132ab2fe29c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1aa1a67f-cc4a-49b5-9b55-04ec3c1fcd6d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<command-message>closeout</command-message>\n<command-name>/closeout</command-name>"},"uuid":"1c149b66-8203-486d-b8e4-fa722b34057f","timestamp":"2026-09-12T13:20:55.251Z","origin":{"kind":"human"},"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills","sessionId":"ca9f8ae1-3064-4ead-9a52-e1c579c0f997","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"1c149b66-8203-486d-b8e4-fa722b34057f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1aa1a67f-cc4a-49b5-9b55-04ec3c1fcd6d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Base directory for this skill: /Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/closeout\n\n# Closeout\n\nOne command that replaces the manual end-of-day sequence: \"any loose ends?\" → \"commit and push what needs to be\" → \"is this in memory?\" → \"write a handoff so Codex can pick this up.\"\n\nRun all five checks, then give ONE verdict. Do not ask permission between steps — the invocation of this skill IS the authorization for the full sequence. Commit and push is standing-authorized for every DEV repo: each repo's `AGENTS.md` Session routine says \"update STATUS, commit, push at end\", and unpushed work on one machine is the top cause of conflicts on the other. The only exceptions are repos whose `CLAUDE.md` says their data must stay local (DexaProject is the precedent); commit those locally and list them as open.\n\n## Step 1 — Loose-ends sweep\n\n- `git status` in every repo touched this session (check cwd first, then any repo mentioned in the conversation; if session context is thin, check `KeystoneOS` and any `DEV/` repo with commits dated today).\n- Unfinished todos/tasks from this session (TaskList if available).\n- Background jobs or workflows still running.\n- Anything the user was promised earlier in the session that wasn't delivered.\n\n## Step 2 — Commit & push\n\n- Every repo touched this session: stage, commit with a descriptive message, `git pull --no-rebase` (the other machine may have pushed), push. If the merge conflicts, keep this machine's version and save the remote copy beside it as `<file>.from-mac` / `<file>.from-windows`, then push and list the file under \"Still open\".\n- Before staging, make sure any new file over 95 MB and any `.env` is in `.gitignore`.\n- Local-only repos (CLAUDE.md says so): commit, do not push, list it.\n- Also check the three config repos, `~/.claude` (dotclaude), `~/.claude/skills` (claude-skills) and `~/.claude/global-memory` (claude-global-memory). If any has changes, commit and push it the same way, so the other machine's `/dev-sync` picks it up.\n- **Push `global-memory` even on a light session.** `daily-backup` pushes it nightly, which is too late for a same-day handoff: work the Mac in the afternoon, sit down at Windows that evening, and anything written to MEMORY.md or handoffs is still only on the Mac. Pushing it here is what makes memory available to the other machine tonight rather than tomorrow. It is the only repo that carries memory across, so treat an unpushed `global-memory` the same as an unpushed project repo: it blocks \"clear to sign off\".\n- Nothing to commit → say so in one line, move on.\n\n## Step 3 — Memory verification\n\n- Check `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log` — must be empty. If not, surface contents and fix the hook issue if obvious.\n- Confirm today's transcript file exists at `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/<today>.md` and was modified within the last few hours.\n- Run the dev-docs harvest so repo docs reach memsearch: `bash ~/.claude/scripts/harvest-dev-docs.sh` (Mac) or `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File $HOME\\.claude\\scripts\\harvest-dev-docs.ps1` (Windows). It copies every repo's `docs/*.md` into `~/.claude/global-memory/dev-docs/`, which is on the index list. One line of output; do this after Step 4 so today's STATUS is included.\n- If this session produced a durable decision or new active thread, update `~/.claude/global-memory/MEMORY.md` (respect the 2,500-char cap; consolidate before adding) or write a Tier A memory file per the memory-system rules in CLAUDE.md.\n- **Tier A does not cross machines — mirror it or lose it.** Project memory lives under a slug built from the project's absolute path, and that path differs on the Mac and the Windows laptop, so a Tier A file written today is not auto-injected tomorrow on the other machine. Global memory and the repo both cross; Tier A does not. So for every Tier A fact written this session, ask: is this durable and project-scoped? If yes, it must also land in the repo — `docs/STATUS.md` for current state, `docs/DECISIONS.md` for a decision and its reasoning, the dated handoff for the detail. Treat Tier A as a fast local cache and the repo as the record. If a fact only ever exists in Tier A, assume the other machine will never see it.\n\n## Step 4 — Cross-harness handoff\n\nThis is the **canonical durable handoff** — the one future sessions and other harnesses read. (For a mid-session, chat-only summary before `/clear`, that's the `session-handoff` skill; the mattpocock `handoff` skill writes to the OS temp dir and is not durable — don't rely on it for cross-session state.)\n\nIf real work happened this session (not just Q&A), write a handoff to\n`<repo>/docs/handoffs/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>.md` (or `~/.claude/global-memory/handoffs/` if no repo fits):\n\n- What was being worked on and why\n- Decisions made (with the reasoning that would be lost)\n- Exact file paths of everything created or modified this session\n- Next actions, most important first\n- Anything mid-flight (open questions, awaited inputs)\n\nPlain markdown, no harness-specific syntax — Codex, Antigravity, or a fresh Claude session must be able to resume from it. Commit it with the Step 2 commit when in a repo.\n\n**Always, in every repo touched (even for light sessions): update `docs/STATUS.md`.** It is the file the next session reads first, on either machine, in any harness. Rewrite the sections in place, keep it short:\n\n- `## Current state` — two to five lines on where things stand today\n- `## Next` — most important first\n- `## Open questions` — decisions waiting on Eric\n- `## Gotchas` — anything that will bite the next session\n\nThe dated handoff file is the detailed record; STATUS.md is the summary. Do Step 4 before the Step 2 commit so both land in the same push.\n\n## Step 5 — Verdict\n\nEnd with a single short report:\n\n```\n## Closeout — <date>\n\n**Committed & pushed:** <repos + one-line summary, or \"nothing to commit\">\n**STATUS.md:** updated in <repos>\n**Memory:** captured ✓ / issue found: <what>\n**Handoff:** <path, or \"not needed — no substantive work\">\n**Still open:** <numbered list, or \"none\">\n\nClear to sign off. / Not clear: <the one thing blocking>.\n```\n\n\"Clear to sign off\" means: every touched repo is pushed (or is a declared local-only repo). If anything is unpushed, the verdict is \"Not clear\" and the unpushed repo is the one thing blocking.\n\nEvery file created or modified during the session must appear somewhere in the report with its full path — \"where did this save?\" should never need to be asked.\n\n## Rules\n\n- Push every touched DEV repo. Do not leave the laptop with unpushed work; the other machine pulls from GitHub, not from this disk.\n- Never skip Step 3 — memory capture failing silently is the user's top recurring worry.\n- If a check fails and the fix is quick and safe (restage a file, clear a stale lock), fix it and note it. If the fix is risky, list it under \"Still open\" instead.\n- Total output should fit on one screen. The user is leaving; brevity is the deliverable.\n"}]},"isMeta":true,"turnCompanion":true,"uuid":"f8db531f-f773-404d-a701-07bf57956852","timestamp":"2026-09-12T13:20:55.251Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills","sessionId":"ca9f8ae1-3064-4ead-9a52-e1c579c0f997","version":"2.1.269","gitBranch":"main"}
